Assignment 2 implementation review
===================================

Review date: 2026-09-18

Files reviewed:
- assignment2.pdf (all 3 pages)
- v1_without_jquery/
- v2_with_jquery/

Overall result
--------------
Both v1 and v2 are present and most functional requirements are implemented. The
main remaining issues are the Bootstrap version/missing links in v1, the filename
mismatch between the PDF and the submitted JavaScript files, and a few minor HTML
quality issues. The previous contents of this report were stale: v2 does exist and
is implemented.

Requirement-by-requirement review
----------------------------------

V1: v1_without_jquery

PASS
- Has four pages: chess.html (home), rules.html, history.html, and about.html.
- Navigation links to Chess, Rules, History, and About are present on every page.
- chess.html contains the required #chessboard placeholder.
- chessboard.json contains the required starting position and is valid 8x8 JSON.
- The board is loaded after page load with vanilla JavaScript AJAX using fetch().
- The table and cells are created dynamically with DOM methods.
- The board cells receive square IDs such as a8 and e2.
- The form is below the board and has src/dst inputs with placeholders e2/e4.
- The Move function reads the controls, moves the source HTML to the destination,
  clears the source square, and clears the inputs.
- The Reset function restores the starting state and redraws the board.
- chess.js passes node --check.

NEEDS ATTENTION
- The assignment explicitly requests Bootstrap 4.4.1 in the head of every HTML
  file. v1/chess.html loads Bootstrap 5.3.3, while v1/rules.html,
  v1/history.html, and v1/about.html do not load Bootstrap at all.
- The PDF is inconsistent about the JavaScript filename: earlier steps say chess.js,
  but later steps say chessboard.js. The submitted code consistently uses chess.js,
  which is coherent, but it does not literally match the later chessboard.js wording.
  If strict compliance is expected, rename chess.js to chessboard.js and update the
  script tags in both versions.
- The PDF suggests Reset should use window.location.reload(). The v1 Reset is
  functionally correct because it restores the saved starting array and redraws the
  board, but it does not follow that specific implementation hint.
- v1/history.html has an invalid closing heading tag: <h2>...</h1>.
- v1/rules.html places a <ul> inside a <p>; the paragraph wrapper should be removed.
- v1/about.html places <hr /> after </body>; move it inside the body.

V2: v2_with_jquery

PASS
- Has the same four-page site structure and navigation as v1.
- All four v2 pages load Bootstrap 4.4.1.
- chess.html loads jQuery before chess.js.
- The page-ready callback calls render_chessboard() and attaches button handlers
  with jQuery .on('click', ...).
- JSON is loaded with $.getJSON().
- Board rows/cells are created with jQuery and inserted with .empty().append().
- Move uses jQuery .val() and .html(), and validates the square format.
- Reset uses window.location.reload().
- v2/chessboard.json is valid 8x8 JSON.
- v2/chess.js passes node --check.

NEEDS ATTENTION
- The same filename discrepancy applies: the code uses chess.js, while the later
  PDF instructions name chessboard.js.

Static verification performed
-----------------------------
- node --check passed for both chess.js files.
- Both chessboard.json files parsed successfully and each contained 8 rows of 8
  squares.
- All expected HTML, JavaScript, and JSON files are present in both directories.

Runtime verification limitation
-------------------------------
I could not complete a live browser/AJAX test in this environment because the
sandbox does not permit binding a local HTTP server. Since fetch() and $.getJSON()
can be blocked when HTML is opened directly as file:// URLs, test both versions
through a local server before submitting. From this assignment directory, run:

    python3 -m http.server 8000

Then verify:

    http://localhost:8000/v1_without_jquery/chess.html
    http://localhost:8000/v2_with_jquery/chess.html

For each version, check all four navigation pages, board rendering, e2 -> e4,
and Reset. Also confirm the browser console has no missing-script or AJAX errors.

Recommended fixes before submission
-----------------------------------
1. Add Bootstrap 4.4.1 to every v1 HTML page and change v1/chess.html from
   Bootstrap 5.3.3 to 4.4.1.
2. Decide whether to keep chess.js or rename it to chessboard.js; if renaming,
   update every script tag in both versions consistently.
3. Fix the v1 history heading, v1 rules list nesting, and v1 about hr placement.
4. Run the local-server browser test described above.
5. Zip both folders together as asg2.zip for submission.
